WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.100
As if we needed to up the stakes in today's
election, as if the country's future wasn't

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.259
already riding on this election.

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:08.969
We have another wrinkle.

00:00:08.969 --> 00:00:14.400
New report by The New York Times, as well
as by Best Leaven in Vanity Fair reveals that

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.510
Donald Trump is not just looking to win because
he is a narcissistic egomaniac.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:26.240
He's also reportedly terrified about going
to prison if he loses today's election.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.000
This is not just based on existing investigations,
but on potential new ones.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.980
He expects, quote from the New York Times
article, Seldom, far from Trump's thoughts

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:41.420
is the possibility of defeat and the potential
consequences of being ejected from the White

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.830
House in unguarded moments.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:49.040
Trump has for weeks told advisers he expects
to face intensifying scrutiny from prosecutors

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.310
if he loses.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:56.170
He is concerned not only about existing investigations
in New York, but the potential for new federal

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.930
probes as well.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:02.610
According to people who have spoken with him,
The New Yorker's Jane Mayer has similar reporting.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.420
She writes, quote, Trump's legal expenses
alone are likely to be daunting.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.090
By the time Bill Clinton left the White House,
he'd racked up more than 10 million in legal

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.090
fees.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:15.190
And Trump's finances are already under growing
strain during the next four years, according

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:17.549
to a stunning recent Times report.

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:22.990
Trump, whether reelected or not, must meet
payment deadlines for more than 300 million

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.960
dollars in loans that he has personally guaranteed.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.079
Much of his debt is owed to such foreign creditors
as Deutsche Bank.

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:35.479
Unless he can refinance with the lenders,
he will be on the hook.

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:37.909
Cornered animals become desperate.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:40.389
Donald Trump is very cornered right now.

00:01:40.389 --> 00:01:44.759
One of the reasons he's desperate to win is
the concern about being prosecuted.

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:49.780
Now, also, fascinatingly, from the New York
Times piece, Donald Trump has people around

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.899
him telling him he's definitely going to win
tonight.

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:53.349
Listen to this quote.

00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:57.530
The president, his associates say, has drawn
encouragement from his larger audiences and

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:02.530
from a stream of relatively upbeat polling
information that advisers have curated for

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.380
him, typically filtering out the bleakest
numbers.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:09.149
On a trip to Florida last week, several aides
told the president that winning the Electoral

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:15.970
College was a certainty, a prognosis not supported
by Republican or Democratic polling.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:21.920
Mark Meadows, chief of staff, has responded
with chipper enthusiasm when Trump raised

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:28.799
the idea of making a late bid for solidly
Democratic states like New Mexico, New Mexico,

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:32.760
an option other aides have told the president
is flatly unrealistic.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.951
This is important because when Trump says
he's winning everything at his rallies, if

00:02:37.951 --> 00:02:42.519
people around Trump are actually telling him,
you've got this, you've got the Electoral

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:43.840
College.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.719
If he doesn't win it, he will definitely think
it was rigged.

00:02:47.719 --> 00:02:52.030
If you're thinking I'm down seven, but maybe
I can pull this off.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:54.599
If you don't win, you sort of are expecting
it.

00:02:54.599 --> 00:03:00.060
If everybody around you is saying you're going
to win the Electoral College and you don't,

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.061
you react very differently and you probably
do all the things we're worried Donald Trump

00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:05.240
is going to do.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:11.390
Now, fortunately or unfortunately for Trump
versus for the country, the country does not

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.659
have a history of prosecuting past presidents.

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:17.680
That suggests Trump doesn't need to worry.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:22.330
But past presidents also haven't had this
level of corruption in their past.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:28.549
So it could change if everything that should
be investigated is investigated whenever the

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:29.890
time comes.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:34.239
The Trump family would likely be tied up in
court for a long time.

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:39.379
To be perfectly frank, probably through the
rest of Donald Trump's life, Trump being prosecuted

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:42.470
would be a tremendously lovely ending.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.659
But Trump out of office is the goal right
now.

00:03:45.659 --> 00:03:48.359
We have the opportunity to do it today.

00:03:48.359 --> 00:03:49.459
And I hope you'll join me tonight.

00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:53.560
I will be streaming live starting at 7:00
p.m. Eastern, 4:00 p.m. Pacific as the results

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:58.830
start coming in on YouTube, Twitch and Facebook.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:56.669
Do not miss it.

